# /etc/udev/rules.d/99-clicklume-keyboards.rules
# Grants the active user RW access to /dev/input/eventN for keyboards so
# clicklume-backend can read hotkeys from keyboard devices without needing root.
#
# Two mechanisms are applied:
# 1. MODE="0660" GROUP="input" — gives the `input` group read/write access
#    to the keyboard device file. User must be in `input` group.
# 2. TAG+="uaccess" — logind may grant session-scoped access on systems
#    that support it (Ubuntu 24.04 currently does NOT for input devices,
#    but this is harmless and future-proofs the rule).
#
# Why two mechanisms?
# -------------------
# Ubuntu 24.04 / GNOME 46 does NOT honour TAG+="uaccess" for input devices
# (see `gotchas/input-group-required-for-evdev-grab.md`). TAG-only leaves
# `crw-rw---- root:input 0660` with no per-user ACL — opening the device
# fails with EACCES for users not in `input`.
#
# MODE="0660" GROUP="input" fixes it for any user added to the `input`
# group. `install.sh` does `sudo usermod -aG input "$USER"`. After the
# next login the autoclicker gets RW access.
#
# Why we filter on ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD
# ----------------------------------
# We MUST limit this to real keyboards only. Granting group-rw on mice,
# touchpads, gamepads, etc. would let any member of `input` (e.g. any
# future accidental member) read those devices too. ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD is
# set by the kernel via 60-input-id.rules based on EV_KEY capability and
# absence of relative axes.
#
# Why we name ourselves "clicklume"
# ---------------------------------
# If you also run another tool that reads keyboards (e.g. a custom keylogger
# for accessibility), put it BEFORE this rule so its TAG+="uaccess" wins,
# or rename this rule to a higher number so it loads after the other.
#
# Install with:
#   sudo cp 99-clicklume-keyboards.rules /etc/udev/rules.d/
#   sudo udevadm control --reload-rules
#   sudo udevadm trigger --property --subsystem-match=input
#
# (clicklume's install.sh can do this for you with sudo.)
SUBSYSTEM=="input", ENV{ID_INPUT_KEYBOARD}=="1", MODE="0660", GROUP="input", TAG+="uaccess"
